%N A400305 Cuban primes p such that p-2 is also prime.
%C A400305 Equivalently, primes p = 3*k*(k+1) + 1 such that p-2 is prime; the terms are the hex numbers A003215 that are the greater of twin primes.
%H A400305 Michael S. Branicky, <a href="/A400305/b400305.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a> (terms 1..500 from Hassane Bakkaoui)
%e A400305 19 is a term since 19 = 3*2^2+3*2+1 is prime and 17 is prime.
%t A400305 Select[Table[3x^2+3x+1, {x, 800}], PrimeQ[#] &&PrimeQ[#-2] &] (* _Stefano Spezia_, Nov 07 2026 *)
%o A400305 (Python)
%o A400305 from sympy import isprime
%o A400305 def agen(kmax):
%o A400305     return [p for k in range(1, kmax+1) if isprime(p := 3*k*(k+1)+1) and isprime(p-2)]
%o A400305 print(agen(720))
%Y A400305 Intersection of A002407 and A006512.
%Y A400305 Cf. A001359, A003215, A028896.
%K A400305 nonn,easy,new
%O A400305 1,1
%A A400305 _Hassane Bakkaoui_, Nov 04 2026
